# ACPENG-3105 -- accepted vulnerabilities
#
# kubectl is pinned to 1.21.14 because the ACP clusters run Kubernetes 1.20.15
# (acp-notprod, acp-ops) and 1.21.14 (acp-ci, acp-test).
#
# The Kubernetes version skew policy supports kubectl only within +/- 1 minor
# version of the kube-apiserver:
#   https://kubernetes.io/releases/version-skew-policy/
#
# With API servers at both 1.20 and 1.21, the only kubectl minors supported
# across the whole estate are 1.20 and 1.21. A newer kubectl would clear the
# CVEs below but would fall outside the supported window, risking spurious
# smoke-test failures against healthy clusters.
#
# Every entry below is a Go standard library CVE compiled into the upstream
# kubectl 1.21.14 binary (built with Go 1.16.15). None are defects in this
# repository's code, and none can be remediated without either:
#   a) moving kubectl outside the supported skew window, or
#   b) upgrading the ACP clusters past 1.21.
#
# REVIEW: when the ACP clusters are upgraded, raise kubectl to match and
# delete the entries below that no longer apply.

